Move an entry into an existing folder, keeping its name, or to a new full
tablet path whose parent exists. rename accepts only a new filename and
keeps the parent folder. A document carries its full-name .mark sidecar.
Occupied destinations, including the target sidecar, are refused before
writing. NFC-equivalent source siblings are refused; --exact selects only the
byte-exact name (absent means not-found). Document/sidecar pairing must stay
unambiguous, including with --exact. These commands take paths, not IDs.
Re-check parents fresh after confirmation (changes: exit 4). Verify
destinations after writing. Twins or a failed listing mean exit 6; the
write is retained, with no rollback.
Ask before changing the cloud; --yes answers. --dry-run lists both paths
without changing anything. Standard output reports the destination.

Usage:
  snctl mv <path> <destination> [flags]

Examples:
snctl mv DOCUMENT/Document/Draft.pdf DOCUMENT/Document/Archive --yes
snctl rename NOTE/Note/Journal.note Diary.note --yes

Flags:
      --dry-run[=true|false]   list document and sidecar changes without writing
      --exact[=true|false]     select only the byte-exact source name; document/sidecar pairing must stay unambiguous
  -h, --help[=true|false]      help for mv

Global Flags:
      --color string            color a table: auto, always or never (default "auto")
      --format string           answer format: table, plain or json (or SNCTL_FORMAT; default: table on a terminal, plain otherwise)
      --json[=true|false]       print answers as JSON (the same as --format json)
      --no-cache[=true|false]   neither read nor write the cache on disk
      --offline[=true|false]    read cached listings and bodies without any request
  -P, --profile string          account profile (or SNCTL_PROFILE)
      --quiet[=true|false]      hide progress lines
  -v, --verbose[=true|false]    log what happens on standard error
  -y, --yes[=true|false]        confirm a command that changes settings or cloud data
